      "hints": [
        "Factorise $(5\\cos\\theta + 4)(\\cos\\theta - 1) = 0 \\implies \\cos\\theta = 1, -0.8$.",
        "Solve in $[0^\\circ, 360^\\circ]$ to find $\\theta = 0^\\circ, 143.1^\\circ, 216.9^\\circ, 360^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Factorise the quadratic in $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$(5\\cos\\theta + 4)(\\cos\\theta - 1) = 0$$\n$$\\cos\\theta = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\cos\\theta = -\\frac{4}{5} = -0.8$$",
        "Find all solutions for $\\theta$ in the range $0^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 360^\\circ$:\n$$\\text{For } \\cos\\theta = 1: \\quad \\theta = 0^\\circ, \\quad 360^\\circ$$\n$$\\text{For } \\cos\\theta = -0.8: \\quad \\theta = 180^\\circ - 36.87^\\circ = 143.13^\\circ \\approx 143.1^\\circ$$\n$$\\theta = 180^\\circ + 36.87^\\circ = 216.87^\\circ \\approx 216.9^\\circ$$\n$$(\\text{Solutions: } \\theta = 0^\\circ, \\quad 143.1^\\circ, \\quad 216.9^\\circ, \\quad 360^\\circ)$$"
      ],
